ch box will also bring you to search results.\nL83: \nL84: Background and more details are available in the cite20†Search & Navigation guide.\nL85: \nL86: [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL87: [Input: Enter a search term or CFR reference (eg. fishing or 1 CFR 1.1)]\nL88: \nL89: [Input: Enter a search term or CFR reference (eg. fishing or 1 CFR 1.1)]\nL90: \nL91:   *   * Details\nL92:   * Print\nL93:   * Search\nL94:   *   * Timeline\nL95:   * Go to Date\nL96:   *   * Published Edition\nL97:   *   * Developer Tools\nL98: ###### eCFR Content\nL99: \nL100: The Code of Federal Regulations (CFR) is the official legal print publication containing the codification of the general and permanent rules published in the Federal Register by the departments and agencies of the Federal Government. The Electronic Code of Federal Regulations (eCFR) is a continuously updated online version of the CFR. It is not an official legal edition of the CFR.\nL101: \nL102: cite21†Learn more about the eCFR, its status, and the editorial process.\nL103: cite22†Title 47 | Telecommunication  | Part / Section\nL104: cite23†Chapter I Federal Communications Commission cite23†0 – 199 L105: cite24†Subchapter A General cite24†0 – 19 L106: cite25†Subchapter B Common Carrier Services cite25†20 – 69 L107: cite26†Subchapter C Broadcast Radio Services cite26†70 – 79 L108: cite27†Subchapter D Safety and Special Radio Services cite27†80 – 199 L109: cite28†Chapter II Office of Science and Technology Policy and National Security Council cite28†200 – 299 L110: Part 200 [Reserved]\nL111: cite29†Part 201 cite30†Executive Policy cite29†201.0 – 201.3 L112: cite31†Part 202 cite32†National Security and Emergency Preparedness Planning and Execution cite31†202.0 – 202.3 L113: cite33†Part 211 cite34†Emergency Restoration Priority Procedures for Telecommunications Services cite33†211.0 – 211.7 L114: cite35†Part 212 cite36†Procedures for Obtaining Internat